# Committed on purpose, same reasoning as apps/cms/.env.production: `next build`
# with output:"export" bakes these into the static bundle, so if they only lived
# in a git-ignored .env.local on one laptop, the deploy would silently ship
# without a way to fetch published articles. Firebase web config is a public
# project identifier, not a credential — the security boundary is
# firestore.rules (a Published article is public read; everything else isn't).
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=AIzaSyBOY4ylBmt2c7JwT6LmeuUosXMLIasDTGY
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=storybridge-eb71e

# reCAPTCHA v3 site key for the contact form (see components/contact-form.tsx).
# Public by design — the secret half lives server-side as the
# RECAPTCHA_SECRET_KEY Firebase secret (functions/src/recaptcha.ts), never
# here. Empty until a key pair is registered at google.com/recaptcha/admin
# for this project's domains (localhost, storybridge-eb71e.web.app, and the
# eventual custom domain) — a console-only step, not done yet. The form
# works without it; see the comment at the top of contact-form.tsx.
NEXT_PUBLIC_RECAPTCHA_SITE_KEY=
